  "attribution_note": "Inherited parent attribution (statements about creating the original source apply to that parent only): Classical equilateral triangular tiling and Cartesian composition. No finite published donor packing. PingYou Ltd supplies the finite whole-strip assemblies and native certificates. This finite transfer uses the explicitly named complete native parent; PingYou Ltd supplies the affine/subdivision realization and certificate.",
  "construction": {
   "name": "common_axis_affine_then_full_axial_subdivision",
   "mechanism_kind": "common_axis_affine_subdivision",
   "proof": "COMMON-AXIS AFFINE TRANSFER FOLLOWED BY COMPLETE AXIAL SUBDIVISION\n\nInherited controls are common_axis_prism_transfer/SOURCE_DECODER.txt and\nreview/constructive/AXIAL_SUBDIVISION_LEMMA.txt. Earlier public axial work\npermits kH=h (and triangle/hexagon base subdivisions with uniform scaling).\nIt does not include this general axial-only common stretch kH/h while\nleaving the canonical base unchanged. Those earlier identities remain\ncontrols and their reviewed cases are included in comparison gates.\n\nFor a complete source of n regular prisms P_h with actual common axis\nR_i e3=epsilon_i d, let k be an integer >=2 with kn<=100. For target height\nH in {1,3/2,2,3}, put r=kH/h and A=I+(r-1)dd^T/(d.d). Apply A to every\ncomplete source owner and center simultaneously. Its owner i is now\nAc_i+R_i P_(kH). A is invertible, so distinct full parents stay disjoint.\n\nFor each complete parent i introduce ALL slots j=0,...,k-1 with centers\n  Ac_i + R_i ((j-(k-1)/2) H e3),\nand the same actual frame R_i. Their closed axial intervals partition\n[-kH/2,kH/2] and their common base is exactly the source/target canonical\npolygon. They are complete height-H owners. The sign epsilon_i is not\nignored: offsets use the actual frame R_i. All sibling pairs have the\nparent axial separator and all cross-parent pairs inherit one transformed\nsource separator A^{-T}u. No independent choice of pair translation occurs.\n\nCompute the full transformed parent union's coordinate bounds from every\nactual canonical source vertex under A. That is exactly the full child\nunion; no axial end cost is dropped. Recenter their common box once, then\napply one common center dilation rho>1 and outward cube restoration as in\nthe reviewed subdivision lemma. Native centers and unchanged quaternions\nare checked on every actual wall and every sibling/cross-parent pair.\n\nThe inverse retains source path/hash/Git provenance and authors, n,k,h,H,\nrational d,A,A^{-1}, common box midpoint and rho, and the complete ordered\n(parent index i, slot j) map. Subtract the inherited axial slot offset and\ninvert A to recover the original parent center. No proper subset or count\nis promoted in the present screen. The bounded k range follows kn<=100,\nnot a coordinate or angle search. The r=1 cases preserve earlier controls.\n",
   "complete_parent_path": "heterogeneous/constructive/root_rectangular_product/public_parents/75b579196e695b12ad0bd04bd136eaa755daf52650cc3479af811f5f81f49e06.json",
